Address Sherlock update audit findings for externalSwap and sequence. (#62)

- sequence now emits SequenceStepFailed for every step failure that does not revert it, making fallback usage and
  primary-route failure reasons visible in logs.
- An expired externalSwap deadline now reverts with the router-wide TransactionExpired error;
  IExternalSwap.DeadlineExpired is removed.
- Consistent naming for the unspent-input refund (unspent, refundAsNative) across interface and implementation.
- IExternalSwap and ISequence documented to the same NatSpec convention as the other router interfaces, including
  how to compose sequence steps from multicall for a native-input swap with fallbacks.